{
	// The tests tree's own resolution context.
	//
	// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. bun resolves path aliases from the NEAREST tsconfig walking up from the
	// importing file. A test under `src` would inherit `.svelte-kit/tsconfig.json`, which SvelteKit generates
	// with `$lib`, `$lib/server` and `$lib/contract` in it. A test under `tests/` leaves that context
	// entirely, and the failure is immediate and loud: `Cannot find module '$lib/…'`. So the aliases are
	// re-declared here, once, rather than rewritten into hundreds of relative paths.
	//
	// WHY NOT ADD THESE TO THE ROOT tsconfig INSTEAD. The root config `include`s `src`, so a
	// `$lib` entry there would collide with the one SvelteKit generates for the same files. Scoping them to
	// this tree keeps the two contexts independent.
	//
	// WHY `$test` AND `$routes` ARE HERE. `$lib` covers `src/lib` and nothing else, so a test naming the shared
	// helpers or a ROUTE handler had no alias to use and counted `..` hops instead. A hop count encodes the importing file's distance from its subject, so it is wrong the
	// moment either end moves — and a wrong path does not always error: anything gating on `existsSync` reads
	// nothing, finds no violations and PASSES. These three aliases delete the whole class.
	//
	// They are declared HERE, in the tests-only context, deliberately: `$routes` resolvable from production
	// source would let a component import a route handler, and `$test` would make test scaffolding bundleable.
	// The app's own resolution never sees them. `$e2e/*` is gone with the tests/e2e tree it pointed at; the
	// Playwright specs reach their own helpers by relative path inside tests/playwright/.
	//
	// `$test` replaced `@encore/test-support` (tests/support/src/, a 333-line two-module tree pretending to be
	// a workspace package — it had no package.json and resolution was always just this path entry). There is
	// no `$setup` any more either: the component-mount harness under tests/setup/ is gone.
	"extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
	"compilerOptions": {
		"baseUrl": ".",
		// `$routes/*` pulls real route files into this program, and a `+page.server.ts` imports `./$types` —
		// which only resolves through the rootDirs overlay SvelteKit's own generated tsconfig sets up.
		"rootDirs": ["..", "../.svelte-kit/types"],
		// OPT-OUT, and a debt rather than a decision. This tree was type-checked by NOTHING until recently
		// (`typecheck` ran app + root only, and the app config excludes `tests/**`), so 284 pre-existing errors
		// accumulated, overwhelmingly `arr[0]` and regex groups inside test bodies. Gating the tree at all is the
		// win; turning this on is a separate pass. Production code does NOT opt out — see the root tsconfig.
		"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false,
		"paths": {
			"$test": ["./helpers.ts"],
			"$lib": ["../src/lib"],
			"$lib/*": ["../src/lib/*"],
			"$lib/server": ["../src/lib/server"],
			"$lib/server/*": ["../src/lib/server/*"],
			"$routes/*": ["../src/routes/*"]
		}
	},
	"include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
